wasi-sh: host builtins — let the embedder register JS-backed command names.

Applied AFTER ash-forkfree.patch, but independent of it: this needs no
fork-free machinery and also fixes a crash that exists either way.

The embedder registers names in JS; find_command() resolves them to a new
CMDHOST and evalcommand() dispatches them in-process, exactly like a
busybox applet — argv in, exit status out, no address space, no wait.
The ABI lives entirely in build/shim/wasistubs.c (host_builtin_lookup /
host_builtin_run), so this patch carries no wasm knowledge.

Hunk 6 is an independent bug fix: a command name containing a slash
(`/bin/php`, `./x.sh`) takes find_command's slash short circuit, reaches
vforkexec(), and dies on vfork()==ENOSYS with "can't fork" and status 2,
ABORTING THE SCRIPT. It now reports 127 "not found" and continues.

--- a/shell/ash.c
+++ b/shell/ash.c
@@ -8520,6 +8520,14 @@
 #define CMDNORMAL       0       /* command is an executable program */
 #define CMDFUNCTION     1       /* command is a shell function */
 #define CMDBUILTIN      2       /* command is a shell builtin */
+/* wasi-sh: a name the JS embedder registered (build/shim/wasistubs.c). This is
+ * a distinct type and NOT a sentinel index inside CMDNORMAL: the applet
+ * dispatch in evalcommand computes applet_no = -index - 2 and indexes the
+ * applet table with it, so any negative sentinel is one reordering away from
+ * running a random applet. It also must never be missed by a switch —
+ * evalcommand's `default:` arm IS the exec path, which here means "can't fork"
+ * and a dead shell. */
+#define CMDHOST         3       /* command is a host (JS) builtin */
 
 struct cmdentry {
 	smallint cmdtype;       /* CMDxxx */
@@ -8770,6 +8778,16 @@
